Hi Evan,

Thank you for your detailed email.

Have you made an inquiry to the landlord since you received the notice of w=
ork order complete on May 8? Is it possible there was a misunderstanding or=
 error made?

As your previous repair file has been closed, we are unable to order the la=
ndlord to do the install at this time. You would need to submit a new repai=
r form to the office to open a file. We will attach a form to this email fo=
r you.

Any time a tenant makes a complaint or repair request, the landlord should =
be investigating and determine if action is needed. A landlord should infor=
m the tenant is a repair is needed and advise how and when repairs will be =
completed. The timeline for landlords completing repairs can vary, if a ten=
ant believes this has gone on longer than what they deem reasonable or unsa=
tisfactory, the tenant can complete a repair form and submit to our office.

I am attaching different policies and fact sheets here for you as well. Add=
itionally, here is the direct link for the tenant page on our website for r=
epairs https://www.gov.mb.ca/cca/rtb/tenant/repairs.html . Here you will fi=
nd most of the documents/policies that are attached and other helpful infor=
mation.

If you wish to submit a new repair request, you are welcome to provide any =
pictured evidence you have available.

Please let us know if you have any questions.

Thank you,

AL/RTB
Client Services Officer
Residential Tenancies Branch
Telephone: 204-945-2476
Fax: 204-945-6273
rtb@gov.mb.ca<mailto:rtb@gov.mb.ca>
